---
/**
 * Exchange — Economics-lens concept at Interactive scale.
 * Consented transfer of value across Surfaces under grants and membrane.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Exchange | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Economics lens · Interactive Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Exchange
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					Consented transfer of value across Surfaces under grants and membrane.
					What moves when one Identity allocates under scarcity and another accepts under ownership.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Core concept under the Economics lens.
						Analogy, not isomorphism. No requirement of fiat, chain, or platform token.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Value crosses only by consent.</h2>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/85">Exchange</strong> is the consented transfer of economic value between Identities.
					Value here means degrees of freedom, access, context advantage, attention, future optionality, or claims under jurisdiction — not classical goods by default.
				</p>
				<p>
					Under the Economics lens, Exchange sits on the Interactive scale.
					The Single scale has already fixed scarcity (relative finitude weighted by Mass), ownership (whose scarcity), preference (ranking), and opportunity (forgone alternative).
					Exchange is what happens when two or more Identities align those structures long enough for a transfer to occur.
				</p>
				<p>
					Every Exchange runs through Interaction Signals, explicit grants, and Space membrane.
					No silent extraction. No transfer that dissolves Refusal-of-Control.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Exchange is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Consented transfer:</strong> both sides (or all relevant parties) accept the movement of claims, access, or outcomes.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Jurisdiction-aware:</strong> what moves is access, grant, or claim under ownership — not possession of another full Identity.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Membrane-bound:</strong> Surface rules, grants, duration, and residual levers still apply.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Opportunity-linked:</strong> each side can compare the transfer against its own opportunity cost before accepting.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Exchange is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a market by itself.</strong>
						A single transfer is Exchange. Market is the collective space in which many Exchanges occur.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not ownership of another Identity.</strong>
						Full possession of another Stem remains excluded.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not silent platform extraction.</strong>
						Attention or data taken without grant is not Exchange under this lens.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not identical with Price.</strong>
						Price is the relative signal; Exchange is the act of transfer under that (or another) signal.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Make consent, grant scope, and duration explicit</strong> before value moves.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Keep residual emergency levers</strong> and human-owner gates on critical transfers.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Compare own Opportunity</strong> with the offered terms before accepting.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Record Exchange events</strong> so both Registries can update claims and opportunity baselines.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/30 p-6">
					<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40 mb-3">Quick self-check</div>
					<ul class="space-y-3 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
						<li>What exactly is being transferred (access, claim, outcome, attention)?</li>
						<li>Under whose ownership and which membrane rules does it move?</li>
						<li>What is each side’s opportunity cost if the Exchange proceeds or fails?</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Related</div>
					<p>
						Prior scale: Scarcity → Ownership → Preference → Opportunity.
						Next on Interactive: <a href="/framework/price" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Price</a>.
						Collective: <a href="/framework/market" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Market</a>.
						Physics parallel: Gravitation and Relativity.
						Biology parallel: Signal and Coupling across boundaries.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/opportunity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Opportunity</a>
					<a href="/framework/price" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Price</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
